## Verified locally — a reproducible working-tree patch that makes this work

I applied this proposal to my installed `dsh-llm-pi-ai` and verified it end-to-end (DeepSeek Harness talking to a CodeBuddy local proxy on the `copilot.tencent.com` compatibility gateway with the `deepseek-v4-flash` reasoning model).

### Two local patches (exactly the `supportsDeveloperRole` pass-through this discussion asks for)

**1. `@deepseek-ai/dsh-llm-pi-ai/lib/index.js`** — one line in `compatProfile` plus one in `resolveModelCompat`:

```js
// compatProfile
const compatProfile = z.object({
    thinkingFormat: z.union(SUPPORTED_THINKING_FORMATS),
    supportsReasoningEffort: z.boolean(),
    supportsDeveloperRole: z.boolean()          // ← added
});

// resolveModelCompat
function resolveModelCompat(provider, entry, route, base, api) {
    const thinkingFormat = entry.compat?.thinkingFormat ?? route?.thinkingFormat;
    const supportsReasoningEffort = entry.compat?.supportsReasoningEffort ?? route?.supportsReasoningEffort;
    const supportsDeveloperRole = entry.compat?.supportsDeveloperRole ?? route?.supportsDeveloperRole;  // ← added
    if (thinkingFormat === void 0 && supportsReasoningEffort === void 0 && supportsDeveloperRole === void 0) return {};
    if (api !== "openai-completions") {
        if (entry.compat?.thinkingFormat !== void 0 || entry.compat?.supportsReasoningEffort !== void 0) invalid(provider, `...`);
        return {};
    }
    return { compat: {
        ...base?.api === api ? base.compat : void 0,
        ...thinkingFormat === void 0 ? {} : { thinkingFormat },
        ...supportsReasoningEffort === void 0 ? {} : { supportsReasoningEffort },
        ...supportsDeveloperRole === void 0 ? {} : { supportsDeveloperRole }   // ← added
    } };
}
```

**2. `~/.dsh/settings.yaml` provider block** (route-level `compat` applies to every model on the route, no per-model repetition):

```yaml
llm-pi-ai:
  providers:
    codebuddy:                       # local proxy / domestic OpenAI-compatible gateway
      apiKeyEnv: CODEBUDDY_API_KEY
      api: openai-completions
      baseURL: http://127.0.0.1:8787/v1
      compat:
        thinkingFormat: openai
        supportsReasoningEffort: true
        supportsDeveloperRole: false     # ← key: force off for non-OpenAI gateways
      models:
        - id: deepseek-v4-flash
          ...
```

### Verified comparison

| State | Request role | Result |
|-------|-------------|--------|
| Before (default URL detection → `supportsDeveloperRole` = true) | `developer` | gateway `finish_reason: content_filter`, `usage=0` short-circuit |
| After (explicit `false`) | `system` | normal streaming response |

The evidence matches the discussion: blocked requests show `usage.inputTokens = 0` and ~1s latency — a request-shape rejection, unrelated to content.

### Why non-OpenAI gateways must set it explicitly

`pi-ai` defaults `supportsDeveloperRole = true` for any standard-looking OpenAI-compatible URL (`!isNonStandard && !isOpenRouter`). A reasoning model (declares `reasoningEfforts` → `model.reasoning = true`) then sends the system prompt as `developer`; domestic gateways such as the `copilot.tencent.com` compatibility layer only accept `system` and answer `content_filter` for `developer`. This patch lets `dsh` opt out explicitly, bypassing the optimistic URL-detection default.

> The patch is lost whenever the npx cache is refreshed (same caveat as the discussion body); use it as a one-time manual fix until upstream merges the pass-through.

Thanks for the clear diagnosis — this provided a concrete, reproducible sample that confirms the root cause.

